Innovation Track — Eureka Operating Model (BU)
Eureka is our standardized platform to submit ideas, assess value/feasibility, and move validated solutions into production.

Tracks (3)

Engineering

AI

AACI (spell out acronym on slide)

Eureka Workflow

Submit ideas in Eureka (problem, value, effort, owner)

Evaluate (impact × feasibility scoring + prioritization)

Experiment (time-boxed PoC / prototype)

Decision Gate: Scale to pilot/production or stop

Production Handoff with clear owner + delivery plan

SPOCs (Governance & Enablement)

2 SPOCs per track

Responsibilities

Review and score ideas in Eureka (impact/effort, risk, dependencies)

Coach idea owners to sharpen scope + success metrics

Drive ideas through workflow stages and remove blockers

Recommend top ideas for prioritization / funding / execution

Effort: 4–6 hours per month per SPOC

Cadence

Fortnightly: SPOC review + prioritization in Eureka

Monthly: Demo/Decision forum — approve Pilot/Production pipeline

Launch

BU kickoff: “How to use Eureka + what good submissions look like”

SPOC onboarding: rubric, templates, and governance playbook
Success Factors

Track leader sponsorship: clear priorities, quick decisions, and visible support for participation

Protected capacity: named contributors with dedicated time for experiments (not “volunteer-only”)

Strong SPOC network: consistent triage, coaching, and fast movement through Eureka stages

Cross-track collaboration: Engineering + AI + AACI co-design solutions; reuse patterns across teams

Clear decision gates: objective scoring + Go/Iterate/Stop discipline to avoid zombie ideas

Path to production: defined ownership, funding, and handoff to delivery teams for scaling

Recognition & incentives: celebrate wins, reward contributors, and publish outcomes monthly
